WEBVTT

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:27.590
That's right. We are known as Charlatan.

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:38.020
Y-You...!

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.230
You...

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.940
...gate-crashers!

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:52.610
Yes, I knew it.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:56.910
I really <i>do </i>know you.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:00.910
I have seen you through
someone else's eyes.

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:06.590
I am almost certain his name was... Louis.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:26.600
THE 
CASE
 STUDY 
OF 
VANITAS

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:34.360
<i>You're pondering the simple things,</i>
<i>pretty much: human emotions, and love?</i>

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:38.740
<i>I hope one day you'll understand</i>

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:43.330
<i>Too many wounds have left you</i>
<i>patched together, a miserable sight</i>

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:48.590
<i>That doesn't even know</i>
<i>the definition of "alive"</i>

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:56.100
<i>No need to say,</i>
<i>"Just the two of us" or anything</i>

00:01:56.100 --> 00:02:04.690
<i>I've a feeling we can understand</i>
<i>each other, and that's fine for now</i>

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:13.650
<i>I love this world,</i>
<i>and the light only you give me</i>

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:18.530
<i>Makes the world I see</i>
<i>through these fractured eyes </i>

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:23.210
<i>Look gleaming and bright</i>

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:27.790
<i>There's no such thing as a sure thing</i>

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:32.550
<i>But you can see me, can't you?</i>

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:41.390
<i>When sky and void meet, look back</i>
<i>because the dreams will come later</i>

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:51.480
Let me introduce you, Noé.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:56.490
These are my darling grandchildren,
Louis and his little sister, Dominique.

00:02:56.490 --> 00:03:01.990
Oh, how wonderful it is that
you're here while Dominique is visiting.

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:05.120
I must once again be off without delay.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:07.710
You may ask these two about this place.

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:09.960
It's nice to meet you, Noé.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:13.880
N-Nice to meet you.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:16.970
It's nice to meet you, too.

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:21.930
Really, Noé? You were raised by humans?

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:22.770
Yes.

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:25.770
So you've been in the
human world the whole time?

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:26.770
That's right.

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:29.060
Where are your parents?

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:30.940
I don't know.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:36.740
My grandma and grandpa said they
found me crying all alone in the snow.

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:38.410
Really?

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:40.990
What a dummy.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.740
You believed what those humans said?

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:44.910
Louis.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.910
They probably abducted you

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:50.670
and were raising you until
you were big enough to eat.

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:52.130
No!

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:55.550
Grandma and grandpa aren't bad people!

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:04.520
They're not.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:12.690
Oh, dear. Oh, dear.

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:15.440
Huh? What's his problem?

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:19.950
Dang it.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:28.870
Sorry about that.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:34.380
There, there. There, there.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:40.180
So after your grandma and grandpa died,
you were taken by kidnappers?

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:45.060
Mm-hmm. I was taken
to all sorts of places.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:48.310
Finally, the Teacher bought me.

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:52.150
<i>Bonsoir</i>, my little one.

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:54.480
Why do you call him, "Teacher?"

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:59.490
When I called him "Master,"
he told me to use "Teacher" instead.

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:03.200
Noé, it must've been so difficult.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:06.160
Are you kidding? I get three meals a day,

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:09.830
and he took me here
to the world of vampires.

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:12.710
It's been so much fun, like a vacation.

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:20.800
You're such a weirdo!

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:30.230
Enough, Louis. It's not <i>that </i>funny.

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:59.880
Louis and Domi were my very first friends.

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:09.890
Are you the ones who live in
that castle deep in the forest?

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:11.430
Mm-hmm!

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:12.560
I'm Mina!

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:13.480
Fred!

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:14.310
Gilles!

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:15.190
Fanny!

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:17.480
Let's play!

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:20.480
We befriended the village children

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:23.150
and even found a secret hideout.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:34.710
Each day was incredibly fun.

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:38.500
What? Really?

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:42.840
You can learn things about people
just by sucking their blood?

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:46.930
Mm-hmm. It's like all these
visions come gushing in.

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:49.390
Wow, that's amazing! Try it on me!

00:06:49.390 --> 00:06:51.930
Really? I can drink your blood?

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:54.180
Hurray!

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:02.440
Huh? I saw lots of myself.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:05.400
Wow, it really does work.

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:09.740
No, I think I'll pass.

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:11.030
Get him, Noé!

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:12.370
Attack!

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:20.790
Well, Noé? Let's have it!

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:29.090
Noé?

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:38.270
I saw Louis all alone,
curled up in the darkness.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:44.230
It made me sad.

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:49.490
If only my power as an Archiviste
had been greater back then...

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:53.410
If only I could have seen Louis' past...

00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:03.130
Domi came to visit each month
from the far-off manor of the de Sades.

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:07.300
Louis, however, spent his days
at the Teacher's castle.

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:11.850
Soon after I was born,
I was diagnosed with a "sickness."

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:16.180
They moved me to Grandfather's castle
so I could get better.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:18.980
A sickness? What kind?

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:20.940
I don't know.

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:23.690
Do you miss your mother and father?

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:25.610
Why would I?

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:30.360
I am dead to the House of de Sade.

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:50.470
Louis?

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:53.100
You're still awake?

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:57.720
Um, is it okay if I sleep
with you tonight?

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:02.020
Louis?

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:07.990
Fine. It's not like I have a choice.

00:09:07.990 --> 00:09:10.240
Great. I'll join you.

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:13.320
You were there, too, Noé?

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:17.830
Huh? What is happening?

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:19.330
What, Noé?

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:22.330
You're scared of thunder, too?

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:26.210
He's asleep already?

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:28.210
Brings back memories, huh, Louis?

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:31.090
The three of us always
used to sleep together.

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:35.180
We're not little children anymore.

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:40.270
I wish I could live here all the time.

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:45.110
Back home, all I do is study
and attend my lessons.

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:49.740
It's far more fun here,
playing with everyone in the forest.

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:52.740
I envy you, Louis.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.790
You shouldn't say that.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:10.130
Once you get older and learn
about the world, you will understand.

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:13.550
You'll understand how much...

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:15.470
...how much...

00:10:15.470 --> 00:10:20.770
...everyone loves and cherishes you.

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:23.600
Mm-hmm.

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:25.190
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:27.480
Darte Datin is so wummy.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:30.690
That's my arm, not Tarte Tatin!

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:32.690
Ow! Let go!

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:34.490
So wummy.

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:37.240
Enough already, you idiot!

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:41.700
Wow, look, Domi!

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:43.750
It's a beautiful blue moon!

00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:46.540
Noé, I'm scared.

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:48.090
It's all right. Look.

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:51.590
I could search the world over
and never find another vampire

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:55.380
who makes such merry at
the sight of the blue moon.

00:10:56.680 --> 00:10:59.430
Grandfather?

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:04.810
What is a curse-bearer?

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:11.860
I found documents about me
in your collection room.

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:16.950
Whoops, I didn't mean
to leave those lying around.

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:22.700
Nice try. You did it on purpose
so that I'd find them.

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:24.200
Hold out your hand.

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:27.460
Is it because I'm one
of those curse-bearers?

00:11:27.460 --> 00:11:33.050
Did my mother and father have Domi
because they wanted to forget me?

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:39.050
Grandfather, what would you have me do?

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:43.850
No, you're mistaken, my dear Louis.

00:11:43.850 --> 00:11:48.060
I do not wish for you to
do anything in particular.

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.310
You are free.

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:53.730
You need only do as you please.

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:55.530
As for me,

00:11:55.530 --> 00:12:02.200
I simply wish to observe your free will
in action and see its results.

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:09.830
What's with him?

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:13.590
That <i>really </i>is in poor taste.

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:17.970
Hey, Louis.

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:19.720
What are you making?

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:21.510
It's a secret.

00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:31.230
Come on, Louis. What are you making?

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:33.940
I told you it's a secret!

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:40.160
After all, it's my gift to you.

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:41.910
I can hardly wait.

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:43.120
Well, try.

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:46.790
I can hardly wait. I can hardly wait.

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:51.540
Looking back, I think it
was around that time

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:55.630
that Louis began to act strange.

00:13:00.930 --> 00:13:03.890
Huh? You're making another one now?

00:13:03.890 --> 00:13:07.890
Yes, I messed up the last one.

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:20.700
Louis, is there something I can do?

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:23.990
What can I do to help you?!

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:30.910
Noé...

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:33.920
I... am...

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:36.380
Louis! Noé!

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:38.840
Domi, is something--

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:43.090
Noé, I just heard the maids talking.

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:44.180
And?

00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:45.430
M-Mina is...

00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:49.140
Mina is to be executed
tomorrow? Is that it?

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:57.150
Mina is to be executed tomorrow?

00:13:57.150 --> 00:13:59.110
But why?

00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:03.320
Why? Because she is a curse-bearer.

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:05.570
A curse-bearer?

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:12.710
They are beheaded by a bourreau.
That's the custom.

00:14:12.710 --> 00:14:16.250
You knew about Mina?

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:21.300
We have to go save her!

00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:23.510
What? Don't be stupid.

00:14:23.510 --> 00:14:24.510
Save her?

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:25.890
How?

00:14:25.890 --> 00:14:28.600
Can you lift the blue moon's curse?

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:30.520
Of course you can't.

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:33.600
No one can save her, Noé!

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:36.360
How can you say that?!

00:14:36.360 --> 00:14:38.860
I merely speak the truth.

00:14:38.860 --> 00:14:41.740
We won't know unless we try!

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:47.410
Go ahead! Try to save her
right here, right now!

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:49.490
Louis.

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:51.790
Listen here, Noé.

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:55.540
There is nothing you can do.

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:59.840
There is absolutely nothing you can do.

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:02.800
Louis, you fool!

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:04.840
Noé!

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:13.180
Noé, I want to save Mina, too.

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:17.020
Might we not help her flee the village?

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:36.540
Mina? What's the matter?

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:44.090
Mina?

00:15:44.090 --> 00:15:46.090
What's wrong?

00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:57.940
Mina? Fred?

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:20.580
Domi, Noé...

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:24.550
I'm so glad you're unharmed.

00:16:24.550 --> 00:16:27.090
Huh? Louis?

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:44.440
Louis!

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:53.120
Gilles... Fanny...

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:56.870
Blood. I want blood.

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:59.620
Blood! Give me blood!

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:07.050
Domi, run.

00:17:07.050 --> 00:17:08.630
Noé?

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:11.010
Blood!

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:12.970
Run, Domi!

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:18.480
Louis, snap out of it!

00:17:18.480 --> 00:17:19.980
What's the matter?

00:17:19.980 --> 00:17:21.940
Are you angry with me?

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:24.900
Because I didn't listen to you?

00:17:24.900 --> 00:17:27.320
Louis! Louis, listen!

00:17:27.320 --> 00:17:29.900
It was all my fault!

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:33.910
Please! I want the old Louis back!

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:51.930
Kill me. I want you to kill me... Noé.

00:17:51.930 --> 00:17:53.470
What?

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:58.180
I'm begging you, Noé.

00:17:58.180 --> 00:18:02.810
I can never return to what I once was.

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:07.110
It won't be long before
a bourreau beheads me.

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:13.990
If I'm doomed to die, Noé...

00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:17.870
If I'm doomed to die, I want you to...

00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:19.750
...kill me!

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:29.170
I can't... Louis.

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:31.840
I could never do that.

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:42.430
Louis.

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:44.140
Louis?

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:46.360
Louis!

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:50.780
You're so smart,
and you can sometimes be mean.

00:18:50.780 --> 00:18:52.530
You're also kind.

00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:55.200
And we were always together.

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:58.080
You are my cherished friend.

00:19:08.920 --> 00:19:11.460
That was a close one.

00:19:12.970 --> 00:19:16.340
I was right to hurry back.

00:19:20.560 --> 00:19:23.600
Are you all right, Noé?

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:48.380
Yes... Teacher.

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:07.640
Louis said he wanted you
to have this when the time came.

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:10.610
He told me to keep it till then.

00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:24.500
Wooden stakes?

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:26.870
It's a secret!

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:29.960
After all, it's my gift to you.

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:41.390
Louis, what did you feel inside
while you were making these?

00:20:41.390 --> 00:20:43.810
Kill me, Noé.

00:20:43.810 --> 00:20:48.020
Take that stake and drive it
through my heart!

00:20:52.860 --> 00:20:54.780
Noé!

00:20:57.110 --> 00:20:59.740
Forgive me, Louis.

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:02.870
I could not save you.

00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:06.830
I could not even kill you
as you had wished.

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:10.330
Forgive me.

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:13.590
Forgive me.

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:16.510
Forgive me.

00:21:18.090 --> 00:21:20.260
Poor thing.

00:21:20.260 --> 00:21:23.970
You were unable to save
your beloved friend.

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:25.680
How very sad.

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:27.770
Is it too much to bear?

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:34.020
Shall I take you to Louis?
Would you like that?

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:37.440
Then you would no longer feel all alone.

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:39.490
Just one thing.

00:21:39.490 --> 00:21:41.660
In exchange...

00:21:42.950 --> 00:21:48.500
...I want you to give me your true name.

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:51.330
I...

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:55.210
There is absolutely nothing you can do.

00:21:58.300 --> 00:21:59.630
<i>Non!</i>

00:22:07.890 --> 00:22:10.140
What are you doing, Noé?

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:13.230
Did you twist your ankle dancing?

00:22:14.520 --> 00:22:16.770
Vanitas.

00:22:19.060 --> 00:22:22.070
Friends

00:23:53.620 --> 00:23:57.080
Questions
